<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
   <meta charset="UTF-8">
   <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
   <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/style.css">
   <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/privacy.css">
   <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg">
   <script>
      window.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", () => {
         document.querySelectorAll(".click-copy").forEach(element => {
            element.addEventListener("click", () => {
               try {
                  navigator.clipboard.writeText(element.textContent);
               } catch {}
            })
         });
      })
   </script>
   <title>Print from your phone online</title>
</head>
<body>
   <%- include("partials/navbar", { privacy: true }) %>
   <main>
      <h1>Privacy Policy for Print From Web</h1>
      <hr>
      <ol>
         <li id="overview">
            <h2>Collection:</h2>
            <p>Print From Web is a web-based file transfer service that allows users to share files directly between devices and in addition, open in the browser for printing saving.</p>
            <p><b>The system is designed to operate with minimal data collection. No user accounts or registrations are required.</b></p>
         </li>
         <li id="operator">
            <h2>Who operates Print From Web</h2>
            <p>Print From Web is operated by an individual developer <b>Soumyadeep Roy.</b></p>
            <p>
               Contact for privacy matters, inquiry, bug reporting, etc:<br>
               <b><span class="click-copy">support.sroy@gmail.com</span></b> (click to copy)
            </p>
         </li>
         <li id="collection">
            <h2>Information Print From Web does NOT collect</h2>
            <h3>Data collection:</h3>
            <p>Print From Web does <b>NOT</b> require or collect:</p>
            <ul>
               <li>Names, emails, phone numbers, or profiles </li>
               <li>User accounts or login credentials</li>
               <li>Personal identification data</li>
               <li>Behavioral tracking or analytics profiles</li>
               <li>Advertising identifiers</li>
               <li>Marketing data collection</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Additionally:</h3>
            <ul>
               <li>Users do not need to register to use this free service.</li>
               <li>Users do not provide personal information through anywhere inside the platform.</li>
            </ul>
            <p></p>
         </li>
         <li id="logging">
            <h2>Logs and technical data</h2>
            <p>Print From Web does not maintain user tracking or analytics logs.</p>
            <p>However, minimal operational logs are generated by for finding and handling errors and stored temporarily on the hosting platform for 7 days.</p>
            <h3>Logged events:</h3>
            <ul>
               <li>Transfer started</li>
               <li>Transfer successful</li>
               <li>Transfer failed</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>These mentioned logs:</h3>
            <ul>
               <li>do not include file contents</li>
               <li>do not identify users personally</li>
               <li>cannot trace any user</li>
               <li>used for finding errors</li>
               <li>are automatically cleared after certain amount of time.</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Additional information:</h3>
            <ul>
               <li>The logs currently appear in hosting platform's (render.com) log senction and deleted after 7 days.</li>
               <li>The logs include Print From Web's server generated messages and timestamps.</li>
               <li>No data is intentionally shared with Render.</li>
               <li>These logs are not used for tracking or profiling.</li>
            </ul>
         </li>
         <li id="stats">
            <h2>Usage statistics</h2>
            <p>Print From Web maintains a single usage data:</p>
            <ul>
               <li>Total number of successful transfers done in the platform</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
               This value increases each time a transfer is successfully done and it is publicly displayed as a global usage indicator.<br>
               It does not link any sensitive information to it.
            </p>
            <p>This is similar measures used in other websites: Total downloads, total files shared, total file convertion etc.</p>
         </li>
         <li id="cookies">
            <h2>Persistent storage usage(cookies and other)</h2>
            <p>Print From Web:</p>
            <ul>
               <li>does not use cookies</li>
               <li>does not use/access local/session storage</li>
               <li>does not use IndexedDB</li>
               <li>does not use any other persistent storage</li>
            </ul>
            <p><strong>Refreshing the page disconnects you from the private connection with the sender/receiver, and clears the temporarily downloaded file(s).</strong></p>
         </li>
         <li id="sharing">
            <h2>Data sharing</h2>
            <h3>User data:</h3>
            <p>Print From Web:</p>
            <ul>
               <li>does not sell user data</li>
               <li>does not share personal data with advertisers</li>
               <li>does not use provide data to marketing networks</li>
               <li>does not use any analytic service or share data with them</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Transferred Files:</h3>
            <p>The files transferred between clients:</p>
            <ul>
               <li>do not go through any third party service</li>
               <li>are not shared with third party individuals/organizations or the hosting platform (currently: Render)</li>
               <li>are not used to train AI models</li>
            </ul>
         </li>
         <li id="security-and-risks">
            <h2>Security, technical issues</h2>
            <p>Print From Web uses standard security protocols HTTP and WSS for file sharing. However:</p>
            <ul>
               <li>No system can be guaranteed completely secure since vulnerabilities may exist in software, networks, or client devices.</li>
               <li>The probability of data exposure is reduced by the absence of persistent data storage and tracking mechanisms.</li>
               <li>Users should only share files with trusted recipients.</li>
               <li>Users should not share confidential files or files containing very sensitive data in this platform</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
               Print From Web is developed and maintained by a single individual. Security improvements may depend on ongoing development and external feedback.<br>
               In rare cases of technical issues, a file may be delivered incorrectly due to connection or routing problems. This is treated as a system reliability issue rather than intentional data handling.<br>
               Users should avoid sending sensitive or confidential content if they require absolute delivery guarantees.
            </p>
         </li>
         <li id="legal">
            <h2>Legal compliance and disclosures</h2>
            <p>Print From Web may comply with applicable legal requests where required by law. Due to minimal retained data, there is generally no personal information available for disclosure.</p>
            <ul>
               <li>No user accounts are maintained</li>  
               <li>No persistent file storage exists</li>
               <li>No behavioral tracking is performed</li>
               <li>Users are not tracable via this platform or collected data</li>
            </ul>
         </li>
         <li id="changes">
            <h2>Changes to policy</h2>
            <ul>
               <li>This Privacy Policy may be changed in order to fit within the local laws.</li>
               <li>Updates will be reflected with a revised effective date.</li>
            </ul>
         </li>
         <li id="transparency">
            <h2>Transparency</h2>
            <p>
               For transparency, I have kept this project source public.<br>
               You can inspect the code in <a href="https://github.com/SoumyadeepRoy2006/print-from-web/tree/deployment/">GitHub</a>
            </p>
         </li>
      </ol>
      <p>If you have any other inquiry, <a href="#operator">contact me</a> via provided email. If required, I will add more information to the privacy policy.</p>
   </main>
   <%- include("partials/footer") %>
</body>
</html>
